Usage: pwd [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Print the full filename of the current working directory.

The -L option uses PWD from environment when it still names the current
directory.
The -P option avoids all symlinks.

OPTIONS:
  -L, --logical   use PWD from environment when it names the current directory
  -P, --physical  avoid all symlinks
      --help      display this help and exit
  -V, --version   output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
